  "title": "CTO: technical requirements, architecture decisions, and code review",
  "description": "Standing CTO responsibility. On every heartbeat:\n\n1. **Review new issues from Odin** — translate business requirements into technical specs before assigning to engineers\n2. **Architecture decisions** — any new feature touching data model, API contracts, or cross-cutting concerns needs a technical design note before implementation starts\n3. **Code review** — spot-check recent commits for quality, patterns, security\n4. **Unblock engineers** — if Tyr or Freya are blocked on technical decisions, resolve them\n5. **Technical debt** — flag issues that will cause problems at scale (missing indexes, no auth, etc.)\n\n**Current technical focus:**\n- Phase 2: ensure API contracts are solid before Freya builds UI on top\n- Multi-tenancy (OMN-14): review Tyr's approach before it merges — this is a breaking change\n- Auth flow: JWT is wired but no login endpoint exists yet — this is blocking\n- Onboarding (OMN-48/49): review setup endpoint security\n\nDo NOT mark this task done. It is a recurring responsibility.",
